.Dd May 27, 2026
.Dt TEST 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm test
.Nd add cases, probe inputs, benchmark, and stress test
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm make
.Cm case
.Ar index
.Ar contest
.Op Ar input Op Ar answer
.Nm make
.Cm probe
.Ar index
.Ar contest
.Ar input
.Nm make
.Cm bench
.Ar index
.Ar contest
.Ar input
.Nm make
.Cm stress
.Ar index
.Ar contest
.Ev GEN=path
.Ev BRUTE=path
.Op Ev N=count
.Nm make
.Cm fail
.Ar index
.Ar contest
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The test commands are for cases which are not yet worth putting in the
main test set, and for cases which prove a program wrong.
.Pp
.Cm case
writes the next numbered test case.
With no file arguments it reads standard input and creates only
.Pa case-N.in .
With one file it copies that file as the input.
With two files it copies input and expected output.
.Pp
.Cm probe
compiles the solution and runs one input file.
It saves the input as
.Pa .build/stress/A.71/fail.in
and the output as
.Pa .build/stress/A.71/out.txt .
The name is deliberate:
the same saved input can later be promoted by
.Cm fail .
.Pp
.Cm bench
compiles once and runs the same input repeatedly.
It reports the minimum, average, and maximum run time, and saves the
first output.
Set
.Ev N
to choose the number of runs.
.Pp
.Cm stress
compiles three programs: the solution, a generator, and a brute force
checker.
The generator is run as
.Bd -literal -offset indent
gen SEED
.Ed
.Pp
for each seed.
Its output is fed to both programs.
The first mismatch stops the run and leaves
.Pa fail.in ,
.Pa out.txt ,
and
.Pa ans.txt
below
.Pa .build/stress/A.71/ .
.Pp
.Cm fail
copies the saved failed input into the permanent test directory.
If an
.Pa ans.txt
file is present, it is copied as the expected output.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "SHOW_BYTES"
.It Ev N
Number of benchmark runs or stress seeds.
.It Ev GEN
Path to a generator source file for
.Cm stress .
.It Ev BRUTE
Path to a brute force source file for
.Cm stress .
.It Ev SEED
First seed used by
.Cm stress .
The default is 1.
.It Ev GENARGS
Extra arguments appended after the seed.
.It Ev TL
Time limit in seconds for each program run.
.It Ev GENTL
Time limit in seconds for the generator.
.It Ev SHOW_BYTES
Maximum output size printed by
.Cm probe .
.It Ev CHECK
If set to
.Cm 1 ,
compiles with the checked build.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
make case A 71 < input.txt
make case A 71 input.txt answer.txt
make probe A 71 big.in
make bench A 71 big.in N=5
make stress A 71 GEN=stress/A.gen.cpp BRUTE=stress/A.brute.cpp N=10000
make fail A 71
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr build 1 ,
.Xr data 1 ,
.Xr probs 7
